TOOL_RESULT retrieve_history:
{"results": [], "n_results": 0}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": [
  "defensive suppression of opponent H2-H1 change",
  "defense as a reliable team trait",
  "team-level defensive effect persistence across seasons",
  "second-half versus first-half scoring change",
  "defensive matchup and counter strategy"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Is a team-level defensive effect on opponent H2-H1 change reliable, measured by split-half or year-over-year stability?",
  "How many team-seasons are needed to detect a stable defensive trait?",
  "Do regression to the mean or selection bias inflate apparent defensive persistence?",
  "How should H2-H1 change be measured to limit score-state, pace and opponent-quality confounding?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [],
 "failed_approaches": [],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "No earlier study by this project was returned for this question, its concepts or its methods, so no prior finding on defensive H2-H1 reliability is established by the retrieval."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Whether opponent H2-H1 change is a reliable team defensive trait.",
  "Whether any earlier project test of this question exists, was run, or failed.",
  "What power, reliability or effect-size benchmarks apply to this measure.",
  "Whether the derived play-type graph records or the matchup-minute files are validated for this use."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The stated unit count of 120 equals 4 regular seasons (2022-23 to 2025-26) x 30 teams, so the primary sample is the full regular-season population with no room for extra team-seasons; playoffs add small, unequal samples.",
  "Year-over-year pairs give about 90 team pairs (3 consecutive season pairs x 30 teams), which limits power to detect modest persistence correlations (roughly r of 0.3 or larger is detectable at 80% power; r near 0.2 is not reliably detectable).",
  "H2-H1 change is a noisy outcome derived from scoring, so a defense's share of it may be small relative to sampling noise and to pace, score-state and opponent-quality effects.",
  "Selecting the best or worst defenses in one season and testing them in the next would be vulnerable to regression to the mean unless the test is pre-specified on held-out seasons.",
  "Rule changes, roster turnover and coaching changes across 2022-23 to 2025-26 may make a team's defense non-stationary, which weakens the 'trait' interpretation."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "No historical records were returned, so there is no evidence on effect sizes, reliability estimates or known failure modes.",
  "The exact definition of H2-H1 (points per possession, margin, or score-state-adjusted) is not given in the task.",
  "Whether the play-type graph and matchup-minute files are complete and consistent across seasons is unverified.",
  "The effect of garbage time and late-game fouling on second-half scoring is unquantified.",
  "The 2025-26 playoff data is labelled complete from 2026-06-21, but its handling in the analysis is not specified."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "The retrieval returned no records, so no earlier result was available to change the decision. The decision rests on the data description and on the sample-size and measurement considerations above."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.45,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
    "text": "120 team-seasons, with about 90 year-over-year pairs, can detect only moderate persistence; small true reliabilities would be missed."
   },
   {
    "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
    "text": "Opponent H2-H1 change per team may have low split-half reliability, so a null may reflect measurement noise rather than absence of a trait."
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "unknown",
  "cited": [],
  "summary": "The retrieval returned no earlier study-family records, so it is unknown whether this question has been answered by this project. No prior work is relied on."
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "Only 120 team-seasons (about 90 year-over-year pairs) limit power to detect modest reliability."
  },
  {
   "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
   "text": "Split-half and year-over-year reliability of opponent H2-H1 change may be low, making a 'reliable trait' conclusion hard to reach either way."
  },
  {
   "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
   "text": "Selecting extreme defenses in one season and testing them later inflates apparent persistence through regression to the mean."
  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Score state, pace, opponent quality, garbage time and lineup mix can move H2-H1 change independently of defense."
  },
  {
   "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
   "text": "H2-H1 change is derived from the scoring outcome, so the defensive effect is entangled with the outcome definition unless possessions and shot quality are controlled."
  },
  {
   "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
   "text": "Several H2-H1 definitions, halves and splits invite selection of the most favourable one."
  },
  {
   "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
   "text": "Roster and coaching turnover and rule changes across 2022-23 to 2025-26 may break the assumption that a defense is a stable trait."
  },
  {
   "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
   "text": "Using full-season or playoff information to define the defensive trait and then testing on the same games would leak the outcome into the predictor."
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.15,
  "rejected": 0.3,
  "untestable": 0.1,
  "artifact": 0.15,
  "uncertain": 0.3
 },
 "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Intra-class reliability of team defensive effect on opponent H2-H1 change (points per 100 possessions allowed, opponent- and score-state-adjusted), estimated as year-over-year correlation of team effects and as split-half reliability within season.",
  "unit": "Team-season (defensive unit), with each game's second-half and first-half opponent scoring as the raw observations.",
  "sample": "Primary: NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 and 2025-26 regular seasons (120 team-seasons, complete data). Secondary and separate: playoffs, reported descriptively only. Exclude 2025-26 playoffs from the primary test.",
  "power": "Pre-specify a minimum detectable reliability of about r = 0.3 with about 90 year-over-year pairs (approximately 80% power at alpha 0.05, two-sided). Report bootstrap CIs; do not claim power for smaller r without a simulation.",
  "controls": "Adjust H2-H1 for opponent offensive quality, pace (possessions per half), score margin at halftime (garbage-time exclusion or win-probability window), home/away and starter-minute mix. Use possession-level rates, not raw points. Shrink team effects with empirical Bayes before any ranking.",
  "falsification": "Placebo outcome: H1 versus H1 split (first half of odd and even games) should show no reliable defensive effect. Permutation: shuffle team labels within season to obtain a null reliability distribution. A nonzero effect on the placebo outcome flags an artifact.",
  "multiplicity": "One pre-specified primary outcome (opponent H2-H1 points per 100 possessions, score-state adjusted) and one primary reliability statistic. Other H2-H1 definitions and split schemes are secondary with Holm correction.",
  "decision_rule": "Supported if the year-over-year correlation and within-season split-half reliability both have 95% CIs excluding 0 and the placebo effect is null. Rejected if the CI for the primary correlation is within roughly plus or minus 0.1 of 0 and the lower bound of a pre-specified equivalence margin is met. Otherwise uncertain. Any placebo effect or permutation-inconsistent result is classed as artifact.",
  "data_version": "NBA stats API per-game files for 2022-23 to 2025-26 regular seasons, as complete at 2026-10-06 (2025-26 regular season complete from 2026-04-13); play-by-play, substitution intervals, starters, matchup minutes and box-score summaries; derived play-type graph used only after its consistency is checked against raw play-by-play; playoffs excluded from primary."
 }
}

